Build 8: GLASS NOTES, HITS AND RING - the melody notes are capsules of glass and the beat hits are glass tiles, each with a dithered pixel light inside (bright at the attack, fading along a note; brightness = velocity), refraction, Fresnel edges, a highlight and a glint; the note or step that is playing lights up. The big TAP TO RECORD ring is a glass tube with a little circuit world inside: an arc of light orbits while idle, the ring fills with light clockwise as the 90 seconds go by while you record (your voice runs round it as a waveform), a quarter lights per count-in beat, an arc spins while Ghost listens. Also fixes the glass taking the faint glow colour's transparency. Version 1.0.4; 493 checks. Build 7: the LIVING GLASS SLIDERS (the owner's brief, Material Study No. 065): STRENGTH, SMOOTH and SWING are now capsules of thick pale-aqua glass sliding over a tiny pixel-art world (circuit towers, waveform, fireflies, traces, sparks, a tiny ghost that sleeps / wakes / follows / celebrates at 100%), lit behind the knob with a Bayer-dithered edge; the glass knob is rendered per pixel (refraction, RGB split, Fresnel, highlight, glint, bubbles, glow, shadow) with spring physics (elastic drag, stretch, jelly wobble, overshoot, release pulse). STRENGTH = electric, SMOOTH = liquid, SWING = groove (bars bounce in the swing you set). Exact parameter values always; drag (Shift = fine), click, double-click = default, wheel, arrows, Home / End; a drag is one automation gesture. SWING now reads 0-100 % (0 straight .. 100 = the old 75 %; the parameter underneath and old projects unchanged; the DAW shows the same 0-100). SWING greys out with QUANTIZE OFF like STRENGTH. GHOST ANIMATION OFF = reduced motion (a still slider). Same layout otherwise. Version 1.0.3; 493 checks. build 6: a TEMPO switch (BPM mode, under the TEMPO row): 1/2x | 1x | 2x of the set tempo, each showing its BPM. The grid, the click and the count-in work at that tempo; DRAG MIDI is written at the set tempo with every time scaled, so it lands in FL exactly as you sang it (2x with QUANTIZE 1/16 = FL's 1/32 grid); the file names say it; saved with the project, a new Ghost Hum starts at 1x. FREE mode keeps its own half / double offers. Version 1.0.2. build 5: opens at 1200 x 760, a size that fits FL Studio's plug-in window on a 1440 x 900 MacBook Pro (still resizable; always this size when it opens), and a new Ghost Hum is always a fresh start: the sounds you TEACH are kept in the project (as before), but a new Ghost Hum no longer reads them from a file shared by every instance. Tested: two at once, the second stays at factory defaults; nothing overlaps at any size. Built and installed on Brandon's own Mac. Version 1.0.1. build 4: better ears, measured on real people (vocadito singers, AVP beatboxers; CC BY 4.0, outside the repo; tests/bench): MELODY note F 0.63 -> 0.67, onsets 26 -> 10 ms, frame pitch 87 -> 96 %, vibrato / slides kept as pitch BEND in PITCH = ORIGINAL (playback, MIDI pitch wheel, the roll draws the line), SMOOTH dial; BEATBOX new ears (log-mel onsets + a small trained net, plain C++): right drum 41 -> 71 %, extra hits 51 -> 20 %, found 83 -> 89 %, with TEACH 77 % (build 3 + TEACH 48 %), kick + hat overlaps, TEACH keeps both ears; EARS: NEW | BUILD 3 keeps the old engines; Basic Pitch / pYIN / CREPE benchmarked (not shipped); HumTests builds and runs on the Mac CI (red if a check fails; it did not build there before); the same synthesised voices on every machine; 442 checks on Linux and Apple Silicon.
build 3: records wherever it is loaded - FL's channel rack (an instrument gets no audio from FL) now works: with no usable host input Ghost Hum listens through the Mac's microphone itself (its own input-only device, opened on the first tap that needs it, at its own sample rate); INPUT AUTO | TRACK | MAC MIC under TEMPO (saved in the state); the status says where it listens and "No sound is coming in" after 2 s; the ring follows the real source; the output is cleared with no input bus; count-in / click still work in the channel rack; smallest window 760 x 600; new input-source checks in HumTests.
build 2: the new look (owner pictures: near-black, green / teal wisps, particles, faint ghosts, glass panels, neon record ring with crackle, glowing ghost logo), FL-style step sequencer (BEATBOX) and piano roll (MELODY) with multi-select / box / Alt-drag / clipboard / arrows, GHOST ANIMATION switch, TAP + HOST tempo, COUNT-IN, ? key commands, hints, speaker click masking, hearing hardened for real mics and mouths, 90 s stop finishes the take, quality pass (rates 44.1-96k, blocks 32-2048, DAW tempo); 346 checks.
